<title>SWEDEN: No Swedish EMU decision for couple of weeks - FinMin.</title>
<headline>No Swedish EMU decision for couple of weeks - FinMin.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Finance Minister Erik Asbrink told a parliamentary European Affairs committee there would not be a decision on Swedish membership of the European monetary and economic union (EMU) for a couple of weeks, former Finance Minister Anne Wibble said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;It will take a couple weeks before I state my opinion about EMU,&quot; Asbrink told a paliamentary European Affairs committee, according to Wibble.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
